.TH tucrc n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tucrc
.PP
Checksum helpers using Tcl core \fBzlib\fR.
.SS API
.CS
set crc [::tclutils::tucrc::crc32 $bytes]
puts [::tclutils::tucrc::hex32 $crc]
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBcrc32 data ?initValue? ?\-encoding binary|utf\-8?\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBadler32 data ?initValue? ?\-encoding binary|utf\-8?\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBcrc32File path\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBadler32File path\fR
.IP \(bu
\fBhex32 value\fR
.SS "Bytes and text"
.PP
\fBcrc32\fR and \fBadler32\fR take bytes by default (\fB\-encoding binary\fR). A character above 255 is \fB{TCLUTILS TUCRC BYTES}\fR on Tcl 8.6 and 9.0 alike; Tcl 8.6 alone would keep only the low byte. With \fB\-encoding utf\-8\fR the text is converted first, and the checksum equals \fBcrc32File\fR of a UTF\-8 file with that text (0.2). See \fBtubase64\fR for why the digests in \fBtuhash\fR default to \fButf\-8\fR instead.
.PP
Errors: \fBBYTES\fR, \fBENCODING\fR, \fBOPTION\fR.
